According to JRBrown  <juliana.rb.brown@gmail.com>:
> 2964.     if (!rn2(13)) {

rn2(13) returns a random value between 0 and 12 (inclusive). If the
value is 0 (1 in 13 chance) then the "if" matches; otherwise, the
"else" part is executed.

> 2965. 	otmp = mkobj(POTION_CLASS, FALSE);

Create a random option.

> 2966. 	if (objects[otmp->otyp].oc_magic) do {
> 2967. 	    otmp->otyp = rnd_class(POT_BOOZE, POT_WATER);
> 2968. 	} while (otmp->otyp == POT_SICKNESS);

This is ugly coding style. The 'while' refers to the 'do'; the 'do..while'
loop is the argument to the 'if'. 'do..while' performs the block at
least once, looping as long as the condition is not met.

Here, if the potion is "magical", it changes its type, using a random
type in the "booze - water" range. The range must be understood
numerically, as relating to the order of declaration of object types
in objects.c. Basically, this is booze, sickness, fruit juice, acid,
oil and water. These also are the "non-magical" potions.

The 'while' condition makes the code loop if the random potion turns out
to be a potion of sickness.

The net effect is that if the randomly created potion is magic, then it
is replaced by a random potion which is not a potion of sickness. Note
that potions of sickness are not magical, so they are still possible,
if the first random creation (line 2965) produced such a potion. The
'while' condition simply makes potions of sickness much less probable
than, say, booze.


Note that chances of finding a djinni in a smoky potion are
decreasing. Chances of a djinni are one in 13+2n, where n is the
number of already created djinnis. If your potions are blessed,
80% of created djinnis will grant wishes. There is an absolute
maximum of 120 djinnis (no more will be created afterwards) so
you will not get more than a hundred wishes or so, you will have
to fight (on average) 6 djinnis, and you will also get (on average)
6 tame djinnis. It will require patience (the PYEC will refuse
to be invoked too often). I fear that a near-infinite source of
wishes may make the game utterly non-fun.


